The bug occurs because if the `inc_rlimit_ucounts` function fails (i.e., returns a value other than 1), the code does not properly decrement the `ucounts` reference counter. This can lead to a memory leak and a use-after-free situation when `put_cred_rcu()` is called concurrently, resulting in accessing freed memory.

